WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.530
Measure results, sell safely, and plan 90 days.

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:08.320
This is the video for module four of Social Media Marketing for Business.

3
00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:17.310
Insights are the numbers the platforms give you about your posts. Without them you are guessing. With them, you do more of what works.

4
00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:24.000
Influencers and partner businesses can bring customers, if you check them and track results.

5
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:31.270
Most Nigerian social selling closes in WhatsApp, so ordering must be clear and payment safe.

6
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:37.760
And a simple 90-day plan, reviewed each month, keeps you focused instead of tired.

7
00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:43.580
Reach is how many different accounts saw your post. It shows how far it travelled.

8
00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:59.760
Engagement rate is engagements divided by reach, times 100. Zainab, who sells beaded jewellery in Kano, had a Reel reach 3,200 accounts with 160 engagements. That is 5 percent.

9
00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:09.910
But a plain product photo that reached only 600 accounts brought 11 WhatsApp chats, because it had a price and a clear call to action.

10
00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:23.210
Platforms cannot see sales in WhatsApp or by transfer, so keep your own sheet: date, platform, post, reach, enquiries, orders and revenue. Ask every buyer where they found you.

11
00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:35.900
Here is a worked example. Ifeoma runs a bakery in Owerri. A local food reviewer with about 15,000 followers, mostly in Imo State, offers to promote her.

12
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:43.310
First she checks. His last 10 Reels get real comments asking where to buy, and most followers are in Owerri.

13
00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:54.140
They agree in writing: one Reel and three Stories for about 40,000 naira, marked as a paid partnership, half paid before posting and half after.

14
00:01:55.390 --> 00:02:03.810
To track results, his followers get a code, OWERRI10, for 10 percent off. Orders using it average about 9,000 naira.

15
00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:18.440
In two weeks, 22 orders use the code, about 198,000 naira in sales. With permission, she reuses the Reel as an ad. Always disclose paid partnerships, and pay on time.

16
00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:26.490
Send the product, price and delivery fee in one message, so the customer sees the full total before paying.

17
00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:30.600
Confirm size, colour and address in writing.

18
00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:39.810
Send payment details to an account in your business name, or a payment link. Then confirm the money in your own app before packing.

19
00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:44.730
Send an order summary, then the rider's name and arrival time.

20
00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:59.930
After delivery, ask for a review and a photo. Patience, who sells children's clothes in Benin City, pinned a short delivery and exchange policy as a quick reply, and the repeated questions and disputes dropped.

21
00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:13.060
Know the common scams. Fake bank alerts by SMS. Edited payment screenshots. Overpayment stories asking you to refund the difference. Links to click to receive payment.

22
00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:20.560
Confirm every payment in your own app before releasing goods, and never share your PIN, OTP or login.

23
00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:28.740
Grow my page is not a goal you can check. And posting daily for two weeks, then going silent, helps nobody.

24
00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:47.230
A SMART goal is specific, measurable, achievable, relevant and time-bound. For example, get 60 WhatsApp enquiries and 20 orders from Instagram between January and March. Three posts a week for 12 weeks beats daily posting and then silence.

25
00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:59.770
Hauwa runs a tailoring shop in Jos, with about 5 hours a week for marketing. Her goal is 90 WhatsApp enquiries and 30 orders from social media in 90 days.

26
00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:06.330
Instagram is her main platform, Facebook support, and WhatsApp Business for orders.

27
00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:14.640
She posts three times a week: one Teach, one Show the work Reel, and one Proof or Offer, all made on Sunday.

28
00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:22.180
She spends about 1,000 naira a day on ads. Her break-even cost per order is 4,000 naira.

29
00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:36.790
On the last Saturday of each month she reviews her sheet and writes three decisions: what to do more of, less of, and new. Mark seasons like weddings, Christmas and Eid, and start promoting two to four weeks before.

30
00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:53.760
To remember. Judge posts by enquiries and orders, not likes. Check partners before paying, and track with a code. Use a business account and a pinned policy. Confirm every payment in your own app. And set SMART goals with a monthly review.

31
00:04:55.010 --> 00:05:03.160
Now write your first monthly report, shortlist three partners, write your ordering and delivery policy, and write your 90-day plan.

32
00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:05.670
Then continue with the lessons below.
